    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0622" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg580"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Lord Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 29, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> This department has reliable
                    information that a vessel is being fitted out at Nassau, in the island of New
                    Providence, to cruise against the shipping of the United States, under the flag
                    of the insurgents. I am consequently directed to request you to call the
                    attention of her Majesty’s authorities there to the subject, in order that a
                    stop may be put to the proceeding.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. HUNTER, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
